  "selected": [
    {
      "id": "cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume.md",
      "sha256": "30d729792e1986dd91c822785512ceabe336ef10a47f0a7db602802e5425d70b",
      "reason": "CMIP6 o2 is stored per unit volume (mol m-3) while WOA23 and the thresholds of 20 and 60 are in µmol/kg, so the models' o2 must be converted before thresholding.",
      "notes_cut": 1,
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Model `o2` is mol m-3 (per volume), while WOA23 and the 20/60 thresholds are µmol kg-1. Convert first: µmol kg-1 = mmol m-3 × 1000 / ρ (ρ in kg m-3). Do not multiply by 1000 and label the result µmol/kg. Without conversion every cell falls below the threshold.",
        "Use the in-situ density (`compute_potential_density_anomaly` with `ref_pressure=None`) for the conversion, not the constant default of `transform_unit`, which errs by about 1 % at depth. State the density used (`attrs['density_assumption']`)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "historical-ssp245-member-continuity",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "pitfalls/historical-ssp245-member-continuity.md",
      "sha256": "02341c56015c6296db14585b4561fc32ca6b4e52e2264bec50eee6746c1d55f6",
      "reason": "CESM2 ssp245 is r10i1p1f1 while the historical is r1i1p1f1, so any historical-to-ssp245 change mixes forced change with internal variability; this is also relevant to the CESM2 no-change handling.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "CESM2 ssp245 is r10i1p1f1 and its parent historical r10 is not in the archive. GFDL-ESM4 and MPI-ESM1-2-LR are r1 in both experiments, so their historical-to-ssp245 change is valid. This is why no CESM2 change can be formed here (Figure 2).",
        "Window differences for GFDL and MPI are 2071-2100 minus 1971-2000 windows from the same member. Do not fit a trend across the 2014/2015 join."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "common-comparison-mask",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/common-comparison-mask.md",
      "sha256": "bbb98200f52b4a692ce097704b8c438179a795a44bec6b856c03cf31931af4ea",
      "reason": "Volumes, thickness maps and the model-vs-WOA23 comparison need one common grid and mask; WOA23's land-sea mask and basin mask must be applied consistently.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "For the maps and any cell-by-cell comparison with WOA23, regrid to the 1° grid and build one shared mask with `build_comparison_mask` (`ocean_only=True` is right since WOA23 is in the comparison), applying it with `.where(mask)`. Report the cell counts.",
        "Volumes, inventories and basin totals are numbers, not cell-by-cell scores. Take them on each source's own grid, not on the shared mask, and say so."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-native-grid-vs-regridded",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-native-grid-vs-regridded.md",
      "sha256": "8ff046ffbadc5794fcd2f8fe93d3bb947c736dec650aa3a3cd6e2412b7da8e68",
      "reason": "Volumes and inventories should be integrated on each model's native grid with its own volcello, and regridding is for the maps and pattern comparison only.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Compute volumes, inventories, basin totals and OMZ thickness on each model's native grid and levels, with its own weights. Regrid (`regrid_horizontal`, 'conservative') only for the maps in Figures 1-2, and state the method.",
        "Integrate thickness-weighted quantities (OMZ thickness, volume) on the original levels. Do not interpolate to the 33 WOA levels first."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-static-grid-fields",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-static-grid-fields.md",
      "sha256": "2ad0548ca0993fa57d8f1fad27a267dcf9c0e1d007a74343d4bbdbf5b4f1ca17",
      "reason": "volcello, areacello and deptho define the cell volumes and thicknesses used for OMZ volume, thickness and the oxygen inventory.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Layer thickness for OMZ thickness and volume is volcello / areacello (`cell_thickness_like`). The `lev_bnds` difference is wrong in partial bottom cells (GFDL-ESM4 volume 1.53e18 vs 1.33e18 m3). No `thkcello`, `masscello` or `rhozero` is available.",
        "Report the `attrs['area_source']` and `attrs['volume_source']` origins. Do not rescale models to a common ocean area."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "missing-values-and-land-cells",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "pitfalls/missing-values-and-land-cells.md",
      "sha256": "f576244f13dde06fed1777eaa9721c68844f61758f66fac704b44f1551e90df2",
      "reason": "Land and below-sea-floor cells carry 1e20 fill values that would dominate volumes and inventories if CF masking is skipped.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Build the valid mask from the `o2` field itself, since masks differ between variables. Use NaN-aware reductions with weights masked to the same cells. Any value near 1e20 is an unmasked fill.",
        "For \"strictly below\" thresholds use `compute_exceedance_fraction` or equivalent, which leaves missing cells out. A raw NaN comparison counts land as not exceeding."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-o2sat-and-derived-oxygen",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-o2sat-and-derived-oxygen.md",
      "sha256": "afe46747641c91aff8ddc9f50165a800a7c64d5d2e39b50e816280d02e59fba3",
      "reason": "WOA23 AOU and percent saturation use their own solubility formula and mass units, which matters for interpreting respiration versus ventilation in the OMZ.",
      "notes_cut": 1,
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Apply the 20 and 60 µmol kg-1 thresholds only after converting `o2` with `identify_oxygen_minimum_zone`, which compares in the field's own units.",
        "Use WOA23's own AOU and percent saturation fields for the OMZ mean. Do not mix a model `o2` with an observed saturation field. Interpret the results with the solubility convention caveat: a high AOU and low saturation point to respiration, while the opposite points to ventilation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "basin-and-region-definitions",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/basin-and-region-definitions.md",
      "sha256": "d0d90c32fab9f6e0a39d4f769a4e902e6412b2ad1b09d9c7d19f6bb3aa426611",
      "reason": "Basin volumes depend on the partition used, here the WOA23 basin mask with marginal seas folded into their parent ocean and the Southern and Arctic Oceans excluded, and this must be stated.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Use the WOA23 `basinmask_01` via `select_basin` with `include_marginal_seas=True`, matching the question's \"marginal seas folded into their parent ocean\". Exclude the Southern and Arctic Oceans, which are separate basins.",
        "For the water column use the choice that a named ocean usually means: surface labels applied throughout (`depth_dependent=False`). Report which was used."
      ]
    }
